## 3. How to give credit

Attribution is the one thing this license actually requires, so here is exactly
what satisfies it. Cite the repository, its author, and — if the point at issue
is that the specification predates the data — the preregistration commit:

> nattobbm (2026). *Intraday Volume Anomaly: the 10:15–10:30 ET Window in CME
> Futures — a preregistered study.* GitHub repository,
> https://github.com/nattobbm/gold-es. Preregistration commit `9a59771`
> (2026-07-23), hash-attested in Bitcoin block 960824 (2026-08-03).

A machine-readable version is in `CITATION.cff`; GitHub's "Cite this
repository" button generates it for you.

## 4. What is not granted

Nothing here transfers authorship. Presenting this work, its specification, its
results, or its data as your own — or republishing it without attribution — is
outside every license above, and the timeline is independently verifiable
(see the *Independent timestamping* section of `README.md`).
